I am having problems all over the place with this. Perhaps it is because I
deleted NFSS2 and its related files before installing latex2e. It seems that
latex2e needs some of those files to run.

Perhaps anyone testing latex2e should do so *without* nfss2 in place, say by
temporarily removing it from TeX' search path when running latex2e. This
might be a better test!

For instance, even \fontencoding{T1} fails with the distribution, for me at
least! It tries to \input nft1.def, which doesn't exist.

Mike Piff

